# Voice-lab: keep the SCRIPTS, never the audio or the models.
#
# The phrase sets are the durable asset — they took real work to build and
# they train every future voice. Recordings are large binaries tied to one
# actor, and models are re-downloadable.
#
# NOTE: this file lives at local-runtime/.gitignore, so every pattern below
# is relative to local-runtime/, NOT the repo root. An earlier version of
# this file used repo-root-style paths (e.g. "local-runtime/voice-lab/dataset/"),
# which silently matched nothing -- confirmed via `git check-ignore`. Fixed
# here; if you add a new rule, don't repeat the "local-runtime/" prefix.

# recordings and their metadata (curated copies live in voice-training/recordings/,
# committed from there instead -- back these raw working folders up separately)
voice-lab/dataset/
voice-lab/dataset-*/
voice-lab/previews/

# downloaded model weights and virtualenvs
models/
venvs/
voice-lab/venv-whisper/
piper/voices/
piper/samples/
piper/previews/
whisper.cpp/
*.onnx
*.bin
*.wav
*.pt
*.safetensors

# runtime state
pitch-config.json
